abstract: >-
  The India Master Water & Geospatial Atlas is a unified, high-resolution All-India
  spatial database combining 75 production GIS layers across administrative units,
  topological drainage basin hierarchies (HydroBASINS Levels 12 to 1), river networks
  (HydroRIVERS Orders 1 to 8), CGWB groundwater extraction and aquifer hydraulic
  parameters (transmissivity, specific yield), GLiM geological lithology, surface water
  bodies (HydroLAKES), 2.6M utility infrastructure assets, and multi-decadal WorldPop
  gridded demographics (2000-2020). Standardized in native EPSG:4326 (WGS 84).
